|Description    ={{en|1=Arms of Woodville/Wydville: ''Argent, a fesse and a canton conjoined gules''. These are the arms of Anthony Woodville, 2nd Earl Rivers, KG (c. 1440 – 25 June 1483), and are visible sculpted in stone within the western entrance of Carisbrooke Castle, Isle of Wight, which entrance was built by him. (Source: The Mirror of Literature, Amusement, and Instruction, Volume 28, p.42[https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=W7wRAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA42&lpg=PA42&dq=woodville+argent+a+fess+and+a+canton+gules&source=bl&ots=U6lQQTfg2u&sig=OCaulWLIhbDrH_6qZhIWPhjHYnA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CDgQ6AEwBmoVChMIvonWks7oyAIVRz0UCh3PuAmS#v=onepage&q=woodville%20argent%20a%20fess%20and%20a%20canton%20gules&f=false])) }}
